{UTF-8}
{ Chapter 17: curves and effects. How strongly does price change demand? One curve, read five ways. }
Effect of price on demand( (0.5,1.6), (1,1), (1.5,0.6), (2,0.4) )
	~	dmnl
	~	Demand relative to normal, at a price relative to normal. Higher price, lower demand.
	|
Relative price=
	1.2
	~	dmnl
	~	Price now, compared with the normal price.
	|
Demand effect=
	LOOK(Effect of price on demand, Relative price)
	~	dmnl
	~	Read the curve normally: with a price of 1.2 demand is 0.84 of normal.
	|
Price for a target=
	LOOK(Effect of price on demand, 0.7, mode=inverse)
	~	dmnl
	~	Read the curve the other way: the price at which demand falls to 0.7 of normal, 1.375.
	|
Steepness=
	LOOK(Effect of price on demand, Relative price, mode=slope)
	~	dmnl
	~	How fast demand falls as price rises, at the price now.
	|
Steps=
	LOOK(Effect of price on demand, Relative price, mode=forward)
	~	dmnl
	~	The curve read as steps (the next point), like a price list.
	|
Beyond the data=
	LOOK(Effect of price on demand, 2.5, mode=extrapolate)
	~	dmnl
	~	What the curve says beyond its last point if its last slope continues: 0.2, still falling. A warning that the data stop at a price of 2.
	|
INITIAL TIME = 0 ~ week ~ |
FINAL TIME = 1 ~ week ~ |
TIME STEP = 1 ~ week ~ |
SAVEPER = 1 ~ week ~ |
